---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import icon from '@assets/installerclean/icon.png';
import scanShot from '@assets/installerclean/screenshots/01-initial-scan.webp';
import unusedShot from '@assets/installerclean/screenshots/03b-details-safe-to-delete.webp';
import confirmShot from '@assets/installerclean/screenshots/04b-Delete-dialogue.webp';
import doneShot from '@assets/installerclean/screenshots/04d-deleted-freed-success.webp';

const downloadPortable =
  'https://github.com/no-faff/InstallerClean/releases/latest/download/InstallerClean-portable.exe';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="InstallerClean"
  description="Clean out C:\Windows\Installer, the hidden Windows folder that fills with old installers. Free, open source, no ads or tracking. Windows 10 and 11."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">
          <svg class="spark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"
            ><path
              d="M16 0c1.3 8.7 6.6 14 16 16-9.4 2-14.7 7.3-16 16-1.3-8.7-6.6-14-16-16 9.4-2 14.7-7.3 16-16Z"
            ></path></svg
          >
          InstallerClean
        </p>
        <h1 class="hero-title">
          <span class="t-path">C:\Windows\Installer</span>
          <span class="t-act">Wipe it clean.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">
          A hidden folder on every Windows PC quietly fills with old installers Windows never clears
          out. InstallerClean asks Windows itself which ones are dead weight and removes only those.
          The scan takes a second or two, and shows you exactly how much space you can reclaim.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <a class="btn-primary" href={downloadPortable}>
            <Icon name="lucide:arrow-down-to-line" class="btn-ic" aria-hidden="true" />
            Download for Windows
          </a>
          <a class="btn-ghost" href="#how">See how it works</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="trust">
          <li><Icon name="lucide:check" class="tick" aria-hidden="true" />Free, MIT open source</li>
          <li><Icon name="lucide:check" class="tick" aria-hidden="true" />No ads or tracking</li>
          <li><Icon name="lucide:check" class="tick" aria-hidden="true" />Clean on VirusTotal</li>
          <li><Icon name="lucide:check" class="tick" aria-hidden="true" />Windows 10 and 11</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <Image class="hero-icon" src={icon} alt="" width={760} loading="eager" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="folder" id="how">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow centred">
          <svg class="spark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"
            ><path
              d="M16 0c1.3 8.7 6.6 14 16 16-9.4 2-14.7 7.3-16 16-1.3-8.7-6.6-14-16-16 9.4-2 14.7-7.3 16-16Z"
            ></path></svg
          >
          The search for help
        </p>
        <h2>If you have searched for help, you know how it goes</h2>
        <p class="sec-intro">
          <span class="mono">C:\Windows\Installer</span> is a hidden folder on every Windows PC. It
          fills with old installers and patches, Windows never clears them out, and Disk Cleanup does
          not touch them. So people go looking for help, and they get told the same few things.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="quotes">
        <figure class="quote">
          <p class="q-text">
            The official Microsoft stance is leave it the hell alone. Far safer to just use the
            built in windows disk cleanup utility.
          </p>
          <figcaption>
            <span class="q-who">DrDan21</span><span class="q-where">r/WindowsHelp</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="quote">
          <p class="q-text">No. Never safe to delete things in the windows folder.</p>
          <figcaption>
            <span class="q-who">tlasan1</span><span class="q-where">r/techsupport</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="quote">
          <p class="q-text">don't mess with it.</p>
          <p class="q-text q-reply">
            They asked what they should do instead. The reply: I just told you.
          </p>
          <figcaption>
            <span class="q-who">the reply to a 60 GB folder</span><span class="q-where">r/techsupport</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="quote">
          <p class="q-text">
            All of the threads I've found tend to recommend the same things which don't solve the
            problem, and then go dead.
          </p>
          <figcaption>
            <span class="q-who">ksparks519</span><span class="q-where">r/Windows10</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <div class="turn">
        <p class="turn-eyebrow">
          <svg class="spark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"
            ><path
              d="M16 0c1.3 8.7 6.6 14 16 16-9.4 2-14.7 7.3-16 16-1.3-8.7-6.6-14-16-16 9.4-2 14.7-7.3 16-16Z"
            ></path></svg
          >
          So is it safe?
        </p>
        <h3>The warning is not wrong. It is just not the whole story.</h3>
        <p>
          Deleting files from this folder by hand, going on names or dates, genuinely can break the
          way Windows updates and uninstalls software. That much is fair.
        </p>
        <p>
          What it misses: Windows itself keeps a record of which files in the folder are still
          needed. InstallerClean reads that record. It removes only the installers for software you
          have already uninstalled and the patches that newer ones have replaced. Everything still
          in use is left exactly where it is.
        </p>
        <p>
          And nothing goes the hard way. Delete sends files to the Recycle Bin. Move puts them
          somewhere you choose. Nothing is touched until you confirm it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="howitworks">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow centred">
          <svg class="spark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"
            ><path
              d="M16 0c1.3 8.7 6.6 14 16 16-9.4 2-14.7 7.3-16 16-1.3-8.7-6.6-14-16-16 9.4-2 14.7-7.3 16-16Z"
            ></path></svg
          >
          How it works
        </p>
        <h2>Run it. See it. Done.</h2>
        <p class="sec-intro">
          Four screens. The whole job, from double-click to space back on disk.
        </p>
      </header>

      <ol class="steps">
        <li class="step">
          <div class="step-text">
            <span class="step-num">01</span>
            <h3>The scan finishes in a second or two</h3>
            <p>
              Double-click the exe. It opens, scans <span class="mono">C:\Windows\Installer</span>,
              and shows what is in use and what is not. No installer, no setup, no wait.
            </p>
          </div>
          <Image
            class="step-shot"
            src={scanShot}
            alt="InstallerClean splash window with the scan in progress"
            loading="eager"
          />
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <div class="step-text">
            <span class="step-num">02</span>
            <h3>See exactly what would be removed</h3>
            <p>
              Every removable file listed with the reason: software you uninstalled, patches that
              newer ones replaced. No guessing on filenames or dates. Nothing changes until you say
              so.
            </p>
          </div>
          <Image
            class="step-shot"
            src={unusedShot}
            alt="The details window listing the unused installer files with sizes and reasons"
            loading="eager"
          />
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <div class="step-text">
            <span class="step-num">03</span>
            <h3>Delete to the Bin, or Move somewhere safe</h3>
            <p>
              Delete sends every file to the Recycle Bin. Move puts them in a folder you choose, so
              you can leave them there a while and check nothing breaks before deleting them for
              good. You confirm, then it commits.
            </p>
          </div>
          <Image
            class="step-shot"
            src={confirmShot}
            alt="The Delete confirmation dialog showing the file count and the space about to come back"
            loading="eager"
          />
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <div class="step-text">
            <span class="step-num">04</span>
            <h3>Done</h3>
            <p>
              You see how much came back, with the restore route in case anything is needed again.
              Bookmark the page and run it whenever your disk gets tight.
            </p>
          </div>
          <Image
            class="step-shot"
            src={doneShot}
            alt="The completion screen with the amount of space freed and the restore hint"
            loading="eager"
          />
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="predecessor">
    <div class="predecessor-inner">
      <header class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow centred">
          <svg class="spark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"
            ><path
              d="M16 0c1.3 8.7 6.6 14 16 16-9.4 2-14.7 7.3-16 16-1.3-8.7-6.6-14-16-16 9.4-2 14.7-7.3 16-16Z"
            ></path></svg
          >
          The predecessor
        </p>
        <h2>PatchCleaner was the answer for a decade</h2>
        <p class="sec-intro">
          When this question first showed up online, the only good answer was John Crawford's <a
            href="https://www.homedev.com.au/free/patchcleaner"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">PatchCleaner</a>. Free, simple, and close to 900,000 downloads since
          2015. Most of what InstallerClean does, PatchCleaner did first. Two things have changed
          since.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <h3>It excludes Adobe by default</h3>
        <p>
          PatchCleaner was built around a list of installers it was confident it could safely
          identify. Adobe's MSP patches did not match cleanly with what the tool was looking for,
          so they were excluded by default. That was the right call in 2016. Today, on machines
          with Adobe Acrobat, the Installer cache is mostly Adobe patches, and this is the comment
          that keeps coming up:
        </p>
        <blockquote class="pull">
          <p>
            I've downloaded Patchcleaner to delete the orphaned .msp files... 29 GB of the files
            are "excluded by filters", so Patchcleaner doesn't seem to help.
          </p>
          <span class="pull-cite">HeatherBunny1111, r/techsupport</span>
        </blockquote>

        <h3>It has been on pause since March 2016</h3>
        <p>
          The developer wrote on a forum in late 2016 about a portable version he was planning, and
          then moved on. The source is closed, so nobody else could pick it up. A decade of Windows
          changes have happened around it, and some antivirus engines have started to flag the 2016
          binary. Nothing is actually wrong with the file, the flags are jumpy ML models reacting
          to old, unsigned, single-developer code, but they are enough to scare people off.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="close">
        InstallerClean is the modern open-source take on the same idea. It detects the Adobe
        patches PatchCleaner skips, it ships on .NET 10, the source is on GitHub, and VirusTotal
        comes back clean across every engine.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="firstmove">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow centred">
          <svg class="spark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"
            ><path
              d="M16 0c1.3 8.7 6.6 14 16 16-9.4 2-14.7 7.3-16 16-1.3-8.7-6.6-14-16-16 9.4-2 14.7-7.3 16-16Z"
            ></path></svg
          >
          For anyone low on space
        </p>
        <h2>Start here. Before anything else.</h2>
        <p class="sec-intro">
          If you arrived here because you searched the folder name, you are already further along
          than most. If you arrived because your disk is full and you do not know where to start,
          you have landed in the right place anyway.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="contrast">
        <div class="vs-card">
          <h3>Disk Cleanup</h3>
          <p>Frees a few hundred megabytes from temp files and old updates. Does not touch this folder.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="vs-card">
          <h3>A disk-tree visualiser</h3>
          <p>Shows you where the gigabytes are. You still have to decide what is safe to delete.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="vs-card">
          <h3>Uninstalling things</h3>
          <p>Slower, less certain, and often leaves the installer files behind anyway.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lead-out">
        <p>
          InstallerClean is the targeted move. One specific folder, with Windows itself deciding
          what is dead weight. From download to space back on disk is about a minute. Worst case,
          you find out you were already clean. No harm done.
        </p>
        <a class="btn-primary" href={downloadPortable}>
          <Icon name="lucide:arrow-down-to-line" class="btn-ic" aria-hidden="true" />
          Download for Windows
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wrap {
    max-width: 1180px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 2rem;
  }

  /* ---------- hero ---------- */
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--c-white);
    padding: 4.5rem 0 5.5rem;
  }
  .hero::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: -20%;
    right: -8%;
    width: 62%;
    height: 130%;
    background: radial-gradient(46% 42% at 62% 40%, rgba(31, 111, 229, 0.16), transparent 72%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .hero-grid {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.04fr);
    gap: 3.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.13em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--c-blue);
    margin: 0 0 1.15rem;
  }
  .eyebrow.centred {
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .spark {
    width: 15px;
    height: 15px;
    fill: var(--c-yellow);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .hero-title {
    margin: 0 0 1.3rem;
  }
  .t-path {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.18rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--c-blue);
    margin-bottom: 0.55rem;
  }
  .t-act {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(2.9rem, 5vw, 4.1rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    color: var(--c-ink);
  }
  .hero-sub {
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.62;
    color: var(--c-body);
    max-width: 33rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.9rem;
  }

  .hero-cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.9rem;
  }
  .btn-primary {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    background: var(--c-blue);
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1rem;
    padding: 0.92rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 11px;
    box-shadow: var(--c-shadow-blue);
    transition:
      background 0.15s,
      transform 0.15s;
  }
  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: var(--c-blue-deep);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  .btn-ic {
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
  }
  .btn-ghost {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    color: var(--c-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1rem;
    padding: 0.92rem 1.2rem;
    border-radius: 11px;
    border: 1px solid var(--c-line-strong);
    background: var(--c-white);
    transition:
      border-color 0.15s,
      background 0.15s;
  }
  .btn-ghost:hover {
    border-color: var(--c-blue);
    background: var(--c-blue-tint);
  }

  .trust {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.55rem 1.4rem;
  }
  .trust li {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--c-body);
  }
  .tick {
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    color: var(--c-green);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .hero-visual {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 420px;
  }
  .hero-icon {
    width: clamp(260px, 32vw, 360px);
    height: auto;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 26px 40px rgba(14, 40, 64, 0.3));
  }

  /* ---------- folder section ---------- */
  .folder {
    background: var(--c-bg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--c-line);
    padding: 5rem 0 5.5rem;
  }
  .sec-head {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin: 0 auto 3rem;
  }
  .sec-head h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--c-ink);
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
  }
  .sec-intro {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--c-body);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .mono {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    color: var(--c-blue-deep);
  }

  .quotes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.4rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
  }
  .quote {
    position: relative;
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--c-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    box-shadow: var(--c-shadow-sm);
    padding: 1.7rem 1.9rem 1.6rem 3.5rem;
  }
  .quote::before {
    content: '\201C';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.7rem;
    left: 1.4rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 3.6rem;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--c-blue-tint);
  }
  .q-text {
    font-size: 1.04rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--c-ink);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .q-reply {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    color: var(--c-muted);
  }
  .quote figcaption {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }
  .q-who {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--c-body);
  }
  .q-where {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--c-muted);
  }

  .turn {
    background: var(--c-blue-tint);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-sky);
    border-radius: 18px;
    padding: 2.3rem 2.6rem;
  }
  .turn-eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.13em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--c-blue-deep);
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
  }
  .turn h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.2vw, 1.7rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--c-ink);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    max-width: 32rem;
  }
  .turn p {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--c-body);
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    max-width: 53rem;
  }
  .turn p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* ---------- how it works ---------- */
  .howitworks {
    background: var(--c-white);
    padding: 5rem 0 5.5rem;
  }
  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4rem;
  }
  .step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .step-text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  .step-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--c-blue);
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .step-text h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.2vw, 1.75rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--c-ink);
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    max-width: 26rem;
  }
  .step-text p {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--c-body);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 28rem;
  }
  .step-shot {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 14px;
    border: 1px solid var(--c-line);
    box-shadow: var(--c-shadow);
  }

  /* ---------- predecessor ---------- */
  .predecessor {
    background: var(--c-bg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--c-line);
    padding: 5rem 0 5.5rem;
  }
  .predecessor-inner {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 2rem;
  }
  .sec-intro a {
    color: var(--c-blue);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-blue-tint);
  }
  .sec-intro a:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--c-blue);
  }
  .prose h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.45rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.25;
    color: var(--c-ink);
    margin: 2.4rem 0 0.85rem;
  }
  .prose p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--c-body);
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
  }
  .pull {
    margin: 1.6rem 0;
    padding: 1.3rem 0 1.3rem 1.5rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--c-blue);
  }
  .pull p {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--c-ink);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .pull-cite {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--c-muted);
  }
  .close {
    margin: 2.4rem 0 0;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.7rem;
    background: var(--c-panel-blue);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-sky);
    border-radius: 14px;
